cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
title: >-
  Ludwieg Automator: LabVIEW automation of a Ludwieg tube wind tunnel
  (vacuum, driver fill, firing and data acquisition)
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-10"
authors:
  - family-names: Reddy
    given-names: MRK
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-8420-6672"
repository-code: "https://github.com/TheWa1kingDead/Ludwieg_Automator"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  LabVIEW application that runs a complete shot of a Ludwieg tube wind
  tunnel. A state machine evacuates the test section and dump tank, fills
  the driver tube in a continuous and a pulsed stage, holds the pressure in a
  band with a thermal-soak timer, fires the fast-acting valve and the camera
  with a hardware-timed trigger waveform, records four high-speed pressure
  channels triggered from the waveform start, and saves the shot with a time
  column. It includes interlocks for driver over-pressure, vacuum gauge
  faults and manual abort, and uses NI PCIe-6374 and USB-6003 hardware
  through NI-DAQmx.
keywords:
  - Ludwieg tube
  - hypersonic wind tunnel
  - LabVIEW
  - NI-DAQmx
  - data acquisition
  - test automation
  - state machine
